Hi Preston,

We are delighted to invite you to participate in the interview process for =
the Senior UX Engineer position at ATPCO. As part of this process, candidat=
es are required to complete a technical assessment project to assess their =
suitability for the role. The assessment evaluates your ability to code a f=
unctional form using Angular (or React), utilizing modified Figma design as=
sets derived from one of our existing products.

Further details regarding the assessment project are provided in the README=
.md file located within the project starter. The assessment is anticipated =
to require approximately 90-120 minutes of your time, and you will be expec=
ted to discuss your work during your interviews.

Access to the project files is provided via a zip archive link: https://atp=
co-uxe-technical-assessment.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/uxe-technical-assess=
ment.zip

You will use this Figma mockup<https://www.figma.com/design/9tdkaFs4cMfI358=
ad5NriK/UXE-Technical-Assessment-Form?node-id=3D0-1&m=3Ddev> for the projec=
t. The password to access it is: atp-uxe

You are welcome to send questions to your recruiter about the project. Thes=
e will be considered as part of your assessment, with quality questions and=
 feedback considered a plus. Please submit your completed assessment by eit=
her creating a repository on GitHub and inviting Galen (gwilk@atpco.net) to=
 join, or by submitting the project as a zip file.

Thank you!


.[ATPCO logo]
.[cid:41813b2c-25ae-4f2b-9a9d-fb05566132dc]

Mia Lemarie

